    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Volunteers can record repeated visitor questions and draft revised room descriptions.\", \"decision\": \"How should room descriptions be improved?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers discuss a room description with visitors while recording their questions and possible revisions. The wording is explored directly with its readers.\nVolunteers collect repeated questions before drafting revised room descriptions. The revisions address demonstrated points of confusion.\nVolunteers draft revised room descriptions and then check which visitor questions still recur. A proposed improvement is evaluated through later questions."
    }
